comments.content:
The NULL check for `texture` now happens after it is dereferenced. `VULKAN_INTERNAL_TextureTransitionToDefaultUsage` is called with `texture` (which internally accesses texture subresources) before the `if (!texture) { return; }` check. If `VULKAN_INTERNAL_CreateTexture` fails and returns NULL, this will dereference a NULL pointer. Move the transition call to after the NULL check:

    texture = VULKAN_INTERNAL_CreateTexture(renderer, false, &container->header.info);
    if (!texture) {
        return;
    }
    VULKAN_INTERNAL_TextureTransitionToDefaultUsage(renderer, commandBuffer, VULKAN_TEXTURE_USAGE_MODE_UNINITIALIZED, texture);

